<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             x:Class="TanMenu.Wpf.Views.Settings.AppearanceCard">
  <!-- Four rows inside one Aero group box: an icon, a title + secondary line, and the control
       trailing. The row SHAPE is Round 5, item 3's spec and is unchanged; the CONTAINER stopped
       being a Windows 11 setting card at Round 7, Task 7 (which deleted the card's fill and
       hairline) and became a Windows 7 property-page group at Task 9. This comment said "Four
       Windows 11 Settings-style rows" until Round 7, Task 10. Populated by ReloadFromConfig — see
       the code-behind for the ReloadFromConfig contract every settings card group follows.

       Each row is a Grid (Auto,*,Auto), not a DockPanel. Built first with a DockPanel per row (icon
       docked left, control docked right, a plain StackPanel as the fill child), the longest subtitle
       of the day — at the time, 按钮大小's (that row, and its even-longer English wording, is gone
       since Round 3, Task 4; the CURRENT longest is 每列个数's English subtitle,
       "Set how many shortcuts each column shows on the Apps page before wrapping to a new one" —
       AppLanguage's ColButtonCountCardSub — longer than 按钮大小's ever was, but the Grid fix below
       still applies to it exactly the same way) — clipped mid-glyph against the ComboBox's left edge
       instead of wrapping onto a second line — confirmed by screenshot, not by inspection. The exact
       DockPanel measure/arrange interaction that produced the clipping was not isolated, so no claim
       is made about it here. Switching to a Grid fixed it: a Grid's star column is guaranteed to
       resolve to the same width at both measure and arrange time, so the middle TextBlock always
       wraps against the width it is actually given, regardless of column order or which sibling is
       docked where. Re-verified by screenshot in both Chinese and English after the change.

       Round 5, item 3: these four rows were already the shape the row spec generalised, so all that
       changed here is that the icon's and the header stack's literal attributes became the shared
       classes tm-card-icon / tm-card-text (Themes/Shell/Launcher.axaml). No pixel moves. -->
  <HeaderedContentControl Classes="tm-group-box" Theme="{StaticResource GroupBox}">
    <HeaderedContentControl.Header>
      <TextBlock x:Name="GroupHead" Classes="tm-group-head" />
    </HeaderedContentControl.Header>
    <StackPanel>

      <Border Classes="tm-card">
        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto">
          <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Classes="tm-icon tm-card-icon" Text="&#xE774;" />
          <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Classes="tm-card-text">
            <TextBlock x:Name="LanguageTitle" Classes="tm-card-title" />
            <TextBlock x:Name="LanguageSub" Classes="tm-card-sub" />
          </StackPanel>
          <ComboBox Grid.Column="2" x:Name="LanguageCombo" Width="220" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                    SelectionChanged="OnLanguageChanged" />
        </Grid>
      </Border>

      <Border Classes="tm-card">
        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto">
          <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Classes="tm-icon tm-card-icon" Text="&#xE793;" />
          <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Classes="tm-card-text">
            <TextBlock x:Name="AppearanceTitle" Classes="tm-card-title" />
            <TextBlock x:Name="AppearanceSub" Classes="tm-card-sub" />
          </StackPanel>
          <ComboBox Grid.Column="2" x:Name="AppearanceCombo" Width="220" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                    SelectionChanged="OnAppearanceChanged" />
        </Grid>
      </Border>

      <Border Classes="tm-card">
        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto">
          <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Classes="tm-icon tm-card-icon" Text="&#xE8D2;" />
          <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Classes="tm-card-text">
            <TextBlock x:Name="FontTitle" Classes="tm-card-title" />
            <TextBlock x:Name="FontSub" Classes="tm-card-sub" />
          </StackPanel>
          <!-- IsTextSearchEnabled restores the WPF list's type-ahead: with hundreds of installed
               families, typing the first letters is how the list is actually navigated. The rows are
               ComboBoxItems whose Content is the display name, so no TextSearch.TextPath is needed, and
               the disabled group-header rows are skipped because they are not selectable. -->
          <ComboBox Grid.Column="2" x:Name="FontCombo" Width="220" MaxDropDownHeight="320"
                    IsTextSearchEnabled="True" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                    SelectionChanged="OnFontChanged" />
        </Grid>
      </Border>

      <!-- Round 3, Task 4: replaces the removed 按钮大小 (小/中/大) row. Nothing on this page names a
           tile width any more — Task 4 fixed every tile at the width that row had called "小" (168 DIP),
           and Round 4, item 3 removed that fixed width too, so a tile is as wide as its own
           icon-plus-label content (see GeneralConfig.ButtonSize's remarks, and TmTileButton in
           Themes/Shell/Launcher.axaml, which carries no Width Setter). This row governs how many
           shortcuts a column holds before wrapping, not how big a tile is. A
           NumericUpDown, not a ComboBox like the other rows here: the value is an integer the user
           picks from a small range, not one of a short list of named choices, and Avalonia ships
           NumericUpDown as a plain control (no extra NuGet package) that already gives a spinner AND
           type-in for exactly that. Range 1–30 matches the pre-Avalonia Blazor build's own numeric input
           for this same setting (docs/plans/2026-06-22-tanmenu-wpf-blazor.md: `min="1" max="30"`) —
           below 1 a "column" is not a column, and 30 comfortably covers even a large 常用工具/folder
           group without inviting a single, absurdly tall column. ClipValueToMinMax keeps a typed
           out-of-range value inside that band rather than accepting it verbatim. -->
      <Border Classes="tm-card">
        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto">
          <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Classes="tm-icon tm-card-icon" Text="&#xE80A;" />
          <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Classes="tm-card-text">
            <TextBlock x:Name="ColCountTitle" Classes="tm-card-title" />
            <TextBlock x:Name="ColCountSub" Classes="tm-card-sub" />
          </StackPanel>
          <NumericUpDown Grid.Column="2" x:Name="ColCountUpDown" Width="220" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                         Minimum="1" Maximum="30" Increment="1" FormatString="0"
                         ClipValueToMinMax="True" ValueChanged="OnColCountChanged" />
        </Grid>
      </Border>
    </StackPanel>
  </HeaderedContentControl>
</UserControl>
